{
  // Next owns this toolchain: it transpiles with SWC and only ever type-checks,
  // so `moduleResolution: bundler` is correct here even though the root config
  // is NodeNext. The two do not have to agree -- they compile different things.
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "lib": [
      "DOM",
      "DOM.Iterable",
      "ES2023"
    ],
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "strict": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "allowJs": true,
    "checkJs": false,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "incremental": true,
    "plugins": [
      {
        "name": "next"
      }
    ],
    "paths": {
      "@/*": [
        "./*"
      ]
    }
  },
  // `include` is Next's, verbatim -- `next build` and `next dev` both rewrite
  // this array, so editing it only makes the tree dirty on the next command.
  // The line that matters is `.next` in `exclude`, and `exclude` filters
  // `include`, so the two globs below match nothing.
  //
  // WHY THEY MUST MATCH NOTHING. Next 16 generates the route types TWICE --
  // `.next/types/` on `build`, `.next/dev/types/` on `dev` -- and both declare
  // the same globals: `AppRoutes`, `ParamMap`, `Routes`. Including both put two
  // copies in one program, and which copy won was decided by which command had
  // run last: `next-env.d.ts` is the first entry here, and Next rewrites its
  // `import "./.next/<dir>/types/routes.d.ts"` to point at whichever directory
  // it has just written. So a `.next/dev` left behind by a dev server could
  // supply the route table a later `tsc` checked against, and typecheck failed
  // with errors in files nobody had touched.
  //
  // That import is the fix, and it is Next's own: one path, rewritten by the
  // tool that owns it. Excluding `.next` leaves it as the only way in, so
  // exactly one copy is ever in the program -- confirmed with `tsc --listFiles`
  // after `dev`, after `build`, and after `dev` then `build`.
  "include": [
    "next-env.d.ts",
    "**/*.ts",
    "**/*.tsx",
    ".next/types/**/*.ts",
    ".next/dev/types/**/*.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules",
    ".next"
  ]
}
